WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.012
The thesis in one slide.

2
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:07.020
On the left, two migrations that happen
regardless: HR moves to Core HCM,

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.163
and identity moves from Active
Directory toward Entra ID.

4
00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:16.337
Meanwhile, the enterprise lifecycle remains
substantially manual and fragmented.

5
00:00:16.337 --> 00:00:18.949
In the middle, what OPM leaves to us.

6
00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.718
OPM fixes the HR side; how
the agency's directories

7
00:00:22.718 --> 00:00:26.762
and ICAM consume that data
is the agency's decision.

8
00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:30.966
And the solicitation requires
SCIM 2.0 provisioning —

9
00:00:30.966 --> 00:00:33.450
exactly what Entra ID consumes.

10
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.247
On the right, the proposal:
start HR-driven identity,

11
00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:42.762
with HR as the source of authority,
expressed in OPM's standard attributes.

12
00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:47.641
So the real choice is: carry ticket-driven
identity through both migrations,

13
00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:53.051
or start HR-driven identity once, while
both platforms are being rebuilt anyway.
